\pard\b\f0\fs24 Europa\b0\f1\fs18\par
\b\f0\par
Population:\b0\f1  Human and sentient industrial presence; exact population not stated.\par
\b\f0 Cities:\b0\f1  No conventional cities described. The story centres on drilling superstructures, buried facilities and worker-bot infrastructure under the ice.\par
\b\f0 Main Characters:\b0\f1  John Walker, G Wolfgang, Nova Serra, Tao Vang, Shai Siante, Tex Kovachnikov.\par
\b\f0 Seasons:\b0\f1  Extreme cold, intense radiation exposure and crushing sub-ice pressure rather than Earthlike seasons.\par
\b\f0 Unique Features:\b0\f1  Thick ice shell over a deep ocean, plume activity, buried worker-bot facilities, hyperbaric chambers, and hydrogen processing tied to the worker-bot program.\par
\b\f0 Sensory Details:\b0\f1  Europa feels industrial, buried and hostile - all steel, pressure control and cold hidden under ice.\par
\b\f0 Sights:\b0\f1  Endless ice, transport pods docking, the buried drilling superstructure, and the suggestion of an ocean roughly 25 km below the surface.\par
\b\f0 Sounds:\b0\f1  Metallic coupling of pods, deep facility hum, drilling infrastructure and filtered atmosphere systems.\par
\b\f0 Smells:\b0\f1  Sterile reclaimed air, coolant, machine rooms.\par
\b\f0 Notes:\b0\f1  In the novel Europa is the next frontier after Ceres and the lost facility. Nova helped design the drilling superstructure there, and the worker-bot program was tested against Europa's radiation and pressure.\par
\b\f0 Built at:\b0\f1  Subsurface human/sentient infrastructure embedded beneath Europa's ice.\par
